WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.890
A standard full-time day is 8 hours.

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.058
A standard full-time week is 40.

00:00:07.408 --> 00:00:13.381
Hours an employee works above either threshold, by day or by week, count as overtime.

00:00:13.381 --> 00:00:15.771
Cisco applies this in every state.

00:00:17.121 --> 00:00:24.630
Overtime is paid at 1.5 times the regular rate for every hour over 8 in a day, or over 40 in a week.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.965
Hours worked on a Cisco-observed US holiday also qualify as overtime.

00:00:30.965 --> 00:00:36.817
Employees enter those hours as hours worked, and Workday treats them as overtime.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:41.325
Hours past 12 in a single day are paid at double time.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.291
Employees need your approval before they start overtime.

00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:54.557
If something unforeseen stops them asking first, they report the hours in Workday immediately and email you as soon as they can.

00:00:54.557 --> 00:00:59.400
Every overtime hour is recorded, whether you approved it in advance or not.
